  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1239 AM CDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nThe strong upper level ridge will eventually break down over the \nnorthern part of the country. However, it will continue to control \nthe weather across the southern states. We will remain under \nsoutheasterly low level flow which will continue to keep hot, moist \nair over South-Central Texas. Additionally we could see some \nseabreeze convection occur daily from Tuesday through Thursday \nmainly over the Coastal Plains, but chances remain rather low. \nOtherwise expect the majority of our area to remain hot and dry with \nhighs in the upper 90s to near 100 each day and lows in the low to \nmid 70s. We could likely see heat indices just shy of heat advisory \ncriteria (108+ degrees) as moisture will remain across the area. \nContinue to check back to future forecasts and remember to practice \nsafe heat safety.",
